      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): surface oversized-file warnings in doctor migration reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThree plugin doctor-contract files read legacy state files during `openclaw doctor` migration with a TOCTOU-prone pattern: `statSync(path)` checks file size (10 MiB cap), then a separate `await fs.readFile(path)` reads the content. Between the stat and the read, a file could be swapped with a much larger one, bypassing the size cap and potentially causing OOM.\n\nAffected files:\n\n1. **Reef** (`extensions/reef/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Two read sites for identity keys and binding registrations\n2. **Active Memory** (`extensions/active-memory/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Reads legacy session-toggle JSON\n3. **Device Pair** (`extensions/device-pair/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Reads legacy notify state JSON\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDoctor migration runs during `openclaw doctor`, triggered by users to diagnose their installation. While the 10 MiB cap is reasonable, the stat-then-read pattern has a TOCTOU race: the stat validates one file's size, but the read may consume a different (potentially unbounded) file. Opening the file first and operating on the same descriptor eliminates this race.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAll three `readLegacy*FileSafely` helpers now use descriptor-bound reads:\n\n```typescript\nconst file = await fs.open(filePath, \"r\");\ntry {\n  const stat = await file.stat();\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(\"not a regular file\");\n  if (stat.size > MAX_BYTES) throw new Error(\"file too large\");\n  return await file.readFile(\"utf8\");\n} finally {\n  await file.close();\n}\n```\n\n- `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle` — `stat()` and `readFile()` both operate on the same descriptor\n- `try/finally` guarantees `file.close()` even when exceptions are thrown\n- Removed unused `import { statSync }` from all three files\n- Warning-aware error path for oversized files preserved exactly\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `statSync(path)` → TOCTOU race: file could be swapped before read | → fd pins the inode; race impossible |\n| Doctor migration with valid legacy state → works | → works (unchanged) |\n| Corrupted oversized file → caught with warning | → caught (unchanged, but without TOCTOU) |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Extension tests pass (active-memory + reef = 462 total):**\n\n```\n ✓ extensions/active-memory (4 test files, 201 passed)\n ✓ extensions/reef (24 test files, 261 passed, 2 skipped)\n```\n\n(Device Pair tests excluded due to pre-existing dependency on an unmerged migration PR.)\n\nThe descriptor-bound pattern is the standard fix for TOCTOU file races — the fd pins the specific inode, preventing substitution between validation and consumption.",
        "branch": "fix/bound-plugin-doctor-migration-reads",
